s.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The search runs once, from an added root joined to every vertex by an edge that costs more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than any set of real edges, so the answer uses exactly one of them when a spanning","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arborescence exists. Self-loops are never weighed; every other edge is weighed once.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m + n log n)."}]}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every weight is finite; the differences between weights do not overflow;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a weight type that is not ","type":"text"},{"code":"SignedNumeric","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the sum of all the weights fits.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum spanning arborescence over every choice of root, by Edmonds’ algorithm; nil when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no vertex reaches every other (or the graph has no vertices).","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"SpanningTrees"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","type":"topic","k